WEBVTT

00:00:00.940 --> 00:00:04.600
If it's not back there, 
then it should be over here.

00:00:04.910 --> 00:00:06.380
Did you throw it away?

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:10.850
I wouldn't throw out an 
inventory list... I think.

00:00:10.850 --> 00:00:11.860
You <i>think</i>?

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:17.180
How could I lose Koura-sama's 
precious inventory list?

00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:20.440
What am I going to do if she fires me?

00:00:20.440 --> 00:00:22.500
Just calm down, Shizuku.

00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:24.370
Huh?

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:26.880
Did you remember something?

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:29.550
No, it's not that.

00:00:30.020 --> 00:00:32.170
Where's Ashiya?

00:00:32.170 --> 00:00:32.970
Huh?

00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:36.090
Shizuku.

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:36.760
Yes?

00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:39.400
Is this the inventory list you're looking for?

00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:40.700
That's it!

00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:42.620
It was in the kitchen.

00:00:42.620 --> 00:00:43.630
Itsuki?

00:00:43.630 --> 00:00:44.810
What's wrong?

00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:50.090
Koura, Shizuku... Sorry, but
I need to step out for a while.

00:00:50.090 --> 00:00:52.030
Where are you going, Itsuki?

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:56.230
I'm going out to find that five-year-old.

00:02:27.370 --> 00:02:32.380
<b>Mystery 5: The Legislative Lake</b>

00:02:28.740 --> 00:02:29.550
Huh?

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:31.290
What?!

00:02:31.730 --> 00:02:34.790
Fuzzy, what are you doing here?

00:02:35.800 --> 00:02:37.300
Hey, runt.

00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:39.400
Are you the thief's friend?

00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:41.870
You're wrong! He's got nothing to do with this!

00:02:42.630 --> 00:02:45.260
If you don't want the runt to get hurt,

00:02:45.520 --> 00:02:48.980
then you'd better behave yourself.

00:02:50.070 --> 00:02:52.130
Fuzzy, I'll be fine.

00:02:52.130 --> 00:02:52.690
Run.

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:54.480
Run away!

00:02:57.820 --> 00:02:58.940
Ow!

00:02:59.210 --> 00:03:00.200
Fuzzy!

00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:01.770
What do you think you're doing?

00:03:05.660 --> 00:03:06.740
Fuzzy!

00:03:07.960 --> 00:03:10.290
You're not going anywhere, thief!

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:10.290
Let go!

00:03:10.870 --> 00:03:11.850
Let go of...

00:03:20.790 --> 00:03:22.970
Looks like you're finally giving it up.

00:03:23.370 --> 00:03:24.260
I understand.

00:03:26.820 --> 00:03:29.180
What? What is this?

00:03:31.180 --> 00:03:32.100
I...

00:03:34.180 --> 00:03:36.730
understand why you're angry.

00:03:37.720 --> 00:03:41.830
But you ignored what I had to say

00:03:42.370 --> 00:03:44.950
in order to say what you wanted.

00:03:44.950 --> 00:03:47.140
You even threatened me with a knife.

00:03:47.140 --> 00:03:50.190
You took out your anger on 
someone else and hurt them.

00:03:50.930 --> 00:03:52.900
Don't you realize

00:03:53.330 --> 00:03:55.930
that was the wrong thing to do?

00:04:04.280 --> 00:04:09.560
Ashiya-kun.

00:04:09.960 --> 00:04:12.310
Abeno-san?

00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:16.000
You left the store without my permission.

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:19.570
What are you doing here?

00:04:20.890 --> 00:04:23.790
<i>He's really mad... No, he's furious!</i>

00:04:23.790 --> 00:04:28.510
What? Did you think I'd greet you 
with a smile, you toddler?!

00:04:28.510 --> 00:04:30.330
I'm not your nursery school teacher!

00:04:28.510 --> 00:04:30.330
Stop, Itsuki!

00:04:30.330 --> 00:04:33.790
Abeno-san, wait! Hear me out!

00:04:30.330 --> 00:04:35.230
<i>This thief said he works for the Mononokean.</i>

00:04:33.790 --> 00:04:38.510
What is it you want to say?
What is it you want me to hear? Huh?!

00:04:35.230 --> 00:04:38.100
<i>If that's true,</i>

00:04:38.500 --> 00:04:40.710
<i>then this blond guy is...</i>

00:04:41.260 --> 00:04:43.740
Itsuki, calm down!

00:04:43.740 --> 00:04:47.470
The master of the Mononokean shouldn't 
be fighting in the street like this!

00:04:47.470 --> 00:04:49.260
Let go! Let go of me, Shizuku!

00:04:49.260 --> 00:04:51.580
Deep breaths, deep breaths!

00:04:49.260 --> 00:04:53.070
Did she just say "Master of the Mononokean"?

00:04:53.070 --> 00:04:54.680
He's the master?

00:04:54.680 --> 00:04:56.270
What's he doing here?

00:04:59.330 --> 00:05:01.200
Who's this yokai here?

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:03.260
You'd better not have made trouble again—

00:05:02.310 --> 00:05:04.820
I didn't do anything! I'm the victim here!

00:05:05.100 --> 00:05:06.450
Oh, right. Fuzzy!

00:05:07.030 --> 00:05:07.800
What?

00:05:07.800 --> 00:05:10.490
Hey, don't just wander off!

00:05:10.870 --> 00:05:13.390
Fuzzy, you don't have to get up.

00:05:13.390 --> 00:05:14.330
Let me see your wound.

00:05:14.590 --> 00:05:16.430
That's the yokai from the other day.

00:05:16.430 --> 00:05:18.830
He's hurt.

00:05:20.080 --> 00:05:21.610
What happened?

00:05:21.610 --> 00:05:23.090
I didn't...

00:05:25.480 --> 00:05:26.270
Can you stand?

00:05:26.270 --> 00:05:26.860
Huh?

00:05:27.670 --> 00:05:30.350
If my employee did something to you,

00:05:30.350 --> 00:05:31.890
please allow me to make up for it.

00:05:32.190 --> 00:05:34.980
What? It's not my fault!

00:05:35.380 --> 00:05:37.120
Shut up, you lost child!

00:05:37.120 --> 00:05:41.540
Y-You're the master of the Mononokean?

00:05:41.540 --> 00:05:43.360
The rumored second master?

00:05:46.480 --> 00:05:47.360
Yes.

00:05:47.760 --> 00:05:53.880
<i>Then this is the guy who "killed" his 
predecessor to become the new master...</i>

00:05:53.880 --> 00:05:58.180
I don't know what kind of rumors they're 
spreading about me on the streets.

00:05:59.330 --> 00:06:01.980
I am the current master of the Mononokean.

00:06:03.860 --> 00:06:07.420
Since my employee seems to be involved,

00:06:07.420 --> 00:06:09.900
I can't just let this slide.

00:06:09.900 --> 00:06:13.560
Blood has been shed, so I'll have 
to report this to the authorities.

00:06:14.750 --> 00:06:17.890
No matter how you look at it, 
this is a clear violation of the rules.

00:06:18.520 --> 00:06:21.740
I hope you'll get off with 
just a fine, but this...

00:06:21.740 --> 00:06:24.320
I... I had nothing to do with this!

00:06:24.320 --> 00:06:25.440
I know nothing!

00:06:25.440 --> 00:06:26.780
I just happened to be here!

00:06:27.180 --> 00:06:29.580
What? What are you talking about?

00:06:29.580 --> 00:06:31.710
I'm busy! I've gotta go!

00:06:31.710 --> 00:06:33.640
Hey! Don't you run away, capybara!

00:06:33.640 --> 00:06:34.280
Ashiya!

00:06:34.280 --> 00:06:35.020
Shizuku-chan...

00:06:35.020 --> 00:06:36.840
Let's hurry back to the Kiyakudo.

00:06:36.840 --> 00:06:38.870
We need to treat this little guy first.

00:06:39.460 --> 00:06:40.200
Yeah.

00:06:43.160 --> 00:06:46.410
They're taking a long time...

00:06:46.410 --> 00:06:49.380
Have they still not found Ashiya-kun?

00:06:53.260 --> 00:06:55.600
Oh? A tadpole line.

00:06:57.800 --> 00:07:00.100
Hello? Who is it?

00:07:00.490 --> 00:07:02.900
Hey, Koura. It's me.

00:07:02.900 --> 00:07:05.370
Oh, my. Mr. Legislator.

00:07:06.050 --> 00:07:07.400
Why the formality?

00:07:08.070 --> 00:07:10.830
When you call me by my job title,

00:07:10.830 --> 00:07:13.410
it makes me think you have 
ulterior motives. It scares me.

00:07:13.410 --> 00:07:16.160
I always have ulterior motives.

00:07:16.160 --> 00:07:19.240
The vocal cords producing 
that wonderful voice

00:07:19.240 --> 00:07:20.720
would make a great medicine...

00:07:20.720 --> 00:07:22.920
Anyway, is Shizuku there?

00:07:23.200 --> 00:07:27.080
Shizuku's out with Itsuki right now.

00:07:27.080 --> 00:07:28.360
With Itsuki?

00:07:28.360 --> 00:07:30.630
He's in the Underworld?

00:07:30.630 --> 00:07:33.310
Yes. He's here buying medicine.

00:07:33.310 --> 00:07:36.620
But the employee he brought 
with him went missing,

00:07:36.620 --> 00:07:38.270
and they're out looking for him.

00:07:38.640 --> 00:07:41.690
Employee? You mean an 
employee of the Mononokean?

00:07:41.690 --> 00:07:43.960
Oh, you haven't heard?

00:07:44.900 --> 00:07:45.770
Really?

00:07:46.210 --> 00:07:51.780
I told Itsuki to let me know when 
he was going to hire someone...

00:07:52.340 --> 00:07:53.420
Hey, Koura.

00:07:53.420 --> 00:07:54.650
Yes?

00:07:54.650 --> 00:07:57.520
Could you give Itsuki a message for me?

00:07:57.520 --> 00:08:00.200
Sure thing. What is it?

00:08:00.980 --> 00:08:03.710
I'll decide whether or not

00:08:03.710 --> 00:08:07.210
to approve the Mononokean's

00:08:08.020 --> 00:08:09.590
new employee.

00:08:10.480 --> 00:08:11.980
That's a rule.

00:08:12.440 --> 00:08:16.970
And he needs to bring him to me immediately.

00:08:17.390 --> 00:08:21.980
<b>The Morose Mononokean</b>

00:08:24.640 --> 00:08:26.780
I understand what happened now.

00:08:27.410 --> 00:08:29.980
Yes. I'm very sorry.

00:08:33.770 --> 00:08:35.990
We've finished treating him.

00:08:36.240 --> 00:08:37.320
Fuzzy!

00:08:37.970 --> 00:08:40.490
Shizuku-chan, how's Fuzzy's injury?

00:08:41.140 --> 00:08:43.150
It's not as bad as it looks,

00:08:43.150 --> 00:08:45.250
so with a little rest, it should heal soon.

00:08:45.580 --> 00:08:47.610
Really? Thank goodness!

00:08:47.610 --> 00:08:49.130
I'm so glad!

00:08:52.610 --> 00:08:53.550
Fuzzy?

00:08:53.900 --> 00:08:56.760
He really likes you, Ashiya.

00:08:57.350 --> 00:08:59.050
Aw, you little...

00:09:02.680 --> 00:09:04.650
Abeno-san, do you want to pet him, too?

00:09:04.650 --> 00:09:09.060
No! Does touching him not 
affect you in any way?

00:09:09.510 --> 00:09:11.150
Huh? You're right.

00:09:11.150 --> 00:09:12.440
I don't feel bad at all.

00:09:13.140 --> 00:09:14.440
Oh, right.

00:09:14.440 --> 00:09:18.820
I have messages for you and 
Shizuku from the Legislator.

00:09:19.840 --> 00:09:21.910
What? The Legislator?

00:09:21.910 --> 00:09:23.370
I have a bad feeling about this.

00:09:23.960 --> 00:09:27.250
What did my brother say?

00:09:27.250 --> 00:09:33.070
For Shizuku, "Come visit Newt 
Lake sometime. I miss you."

00:09:33.070 --> 00:09:34.840
But I just saw him yesterday!

00:09:34.840 --> 00:09:36.270
<i>Does he get lonely a lot?</i>

00:09:36.270 --> 00:09:37.590
And for Itsuki...

00:09:38.200 --> 00:09:41.820
"I'll decide whether or not to approve 
the Mononokean's new employee.

00:09:41.820 --> 00:09:42.930
That's a rule.

00:09:43.890 --> 00:09:48.560
Bring him to me immediately."

00:09:48.560 --> 00:09:51.050
What? Seriously?

00:09:51.050 --> 00:09:55.080
He's the one who made the rule allowing 
masters to choose their own employees!

00:09:56.100 --> 00:09:59.080
There's no point in complaining to me about it.

00:09:59.080 --> 00:10:02.120
Why did the Legislator 
suddenly say he'd decide?

00:10:02.760 --> 00:10:08.800
Itsuki, you didn't tell the Legislator 
you hired an employee, did you?

00:10:08.800 --> 00:10:10.580
He was sulking about it.

00:10:10.860 --> 00:10:12.300
That's why?

00:10:15.090 --> 00:10:16.840
We have no choice. Let's go.

00:10:16.840 --> 00:10:18.140
Go where?

00:10:18.140 --> 00:10:20.590
To Newt Lake, to the see the Legislator.

00:10:21.000 --> 00:10:25.020
Who is this Legislator?

00:10:25.410 --> 00:10:28.350
Ashiya, you don't know about my brother?

00:10:28.350 --> 00:10:31.470
The Legislator is my superior.

00:10:31.470 --> 00:10:32.440
Your superior?

00:10:32.800 --> 00:10:36.330
He's one of three influential figures

00:10:36.330 --> 00:10:38.450
who manage the Underworld.

00:10:38.450 --> 00:10:41.020
What? And we're going to see him?

00:10:41.020 --> 00:10:42.860
In that case,

00:10:43.380 --> 00:10:46.960
I'll give you the bit of 
medicine we've made so far.

00:10:46.960 --> 00:10:51.250
Thanks. Oh, could you also throw 
in a healing salve with that?

00:10:51.520 --> 00:10:52.670
A healing salve?

00:10:53.120 --> 00:10:54.600
For the hairball.

00:10:55.010 --> 00:10:58.100
Can we take Fuzzy back to the Mononokean?

00:10:58.720 --> 00:11:01.320
We have to keep an eye on him until he heals.

00:11:01.320 --> 00:11:03.520
You'd better take good care of him.

00:11:03.520 --> 00:11:06.060
I will! I'll take real good—huh?

00:11:06.760 --> 00:11:07.790
He's asleep?

00:11:07.790 --> 00:11:09.610
He's really taken to you.

00:11:10.370 --> 00:11:13.230
He must feel safe around Ashiya.

00:11:20.210 --> 00:11:21.950
Here's the medicine.

00:11:22.760 --> 00:11:25.240
I'll make extra for your next visit.

00:11:25.240 --> 00:11:25.950
Thanks.

00:11:27.270 --> 00:11:29.710
<i>That medicine must really be important.</i>

00:11:30.010 --> 00:11:32.240
Have a safe trip.

00:11:32.240 --> 00:11:34.250
Come see us again.

00:11:35.020 --> 00:11:37.710
I will. Thanks for all your help.

00:11:38.850 --> 00:11:40.720
Aside from the Legislator,

00:11:40.720 --> 00:11:42.570
there's the Justice and the Executive.

00:11:42.570 --> 00:11:45.030
They're the Underworld's top three figures.

00:11:45.640 --> 00:11:48.860
The Legislator has the power to 
make rules in the Underworld.

00:11:49.560 --> 00:11:52.250
Anyone who breaks those rules is punished.

00:11:52.730 --> 00:11:56.230
The Underworld's punishment? 
That sounds terrifying.

00:11:56.510 --> 00:11:59.270
But the master of the 
Mononokean is an exception.

00:11:59.810 --> 00:12:03.740
He's exempt from all rules.

00:12:04.260 --> 00:12:08.650
So you're free to run wild 
and do whatever you want?

00:12:09.060 --> 00:12:11.400
Run wild? What am I, a dog?

00:12:11.400 --> 00:12:14.750
And there is one rule that 
applies to the master.

00:12:15.140 --> 00:12:16.410
Just one?

00:12:16.410 --> 00:12:21.260
"The master must follow any rules directly 
given to him by the Legislator."

00:12:21.650 --> 00:12:23.200
If I break that rule,

00:12:23.200 --> 00:12:25.510
I could lose my position as the master.

00:12:26.010 --> 00:12:29.430
<i>That explains it... But still...</i>

00:12:29.430 --> 00:12:30.850
It's so far!

00:12:31.240 --> 00:12:34.330
We haven't even been following a path!

00:12:34.330 --> 00:12:36.230
Are you sure we're not lost?

00:12:36.870 --> 00:12:39.680
Shut up. This is a shortcut.

00:12:39.680 --> 00:12:42.240
Besides, Newt Lake is just ahead.

00:12:42.560 --> 00:12:46.470
And the Legislator is at Newt Lake, right?

00:12:46.470 --> 00:12:47.240
Yeah.

00:12:47.240 --> 00:12:51.750
What kind of yokai is the 
Legislator of Newt Lake?

00:12:52.120 --> 00:12:55.120
Huh? What kind? Well...

00:12:55.120 --> 00:12:59.040
He's a chain-smoking, alcoholic 
sex maniac who loves gambling.

00:12:59.460 --> 00:13:03.930
The backbone of the Underworld is 
upheld by such an unreliable character?

00:13:03.930 --> 00:13:05.530
Oh, he's also in love with his sister.

00:13:06.520 --> 00:13:11.840
And he's going to judge whether I'm 
worthy of working for the Mononokean?

00:13:11.840 --> 00:13:13.320
Unfortunately, yes.

00:13:14.260 --> 00:13:17.020
I'd be bummed if he fired me.

00:13:17.020 --> 00:13:17.770
Fired you?

00:13:18.240 --> 00:13:21.230
What are you talking about? 
I won't let him fire you.

00:13:21.230 --> 00:13:25.480
Abeno-san, despite everything 
you say, you do depend on me!

00:13:25.480 --> 00:13:28.680
No. Don't forget you have a debt to repay.

00:13:28.680 --> 00:13:29.780
Oh, right.

00:13:31.790 --> 00:13:33.080
We're here.

00:13:37.080 --> 00:13:39.380
This is Newt Lake?

00:13:45.480 --> 00:13:47.350
It's been a while, Legislator.

00:13:47.350 --> 00:13:49.550
You finally came, Itsuki.

00:13:49.870 --> 00:13:52.830
And you brought your new employee.

00:13:52.830 --> 00:13:55.320
Welcome to Newt Lake.

00:13:56.060 --> 00:13:58.310
<i>This is the Legislator?</i>

00:13:58.310 --> 00:14:00.020
Hup...

00:14:01.520 --> 00:14:02.950
What's wrong, Fuzzy?

00:14:04.610 --> 00:14:09.070
I entrusted Itsuki with hiring 
employees for the Mononokean,

00:14:09.400 --> 00:14:13.580
but it looks like he chose a rather weak one.

00:14:19.110 --> 00:14:22.990
Nope, not good enough. 
You should quit this job.

00:14:22.990 --> 00:14:23.630
What?

00:14:24.350 --> 00:14:26.970
Hey, you can't just say that!

00:14:26.970 --> 00:14:30.310
But it's not possible for 
this kid to handle the job.

00:14:30.720 --> 00:14:31.970
Besides,

00:14:33.120 --> 00:14:34.350
he's a human.

00:14:39.120 --> 00:14:40.770
<i>He knows I'm a human?!</i>

00:14:40.770 --> 00:14:41.760
Right?

00:14:41.760 --> 00:14:44.520
I-I'm not! I'm just, uh...

00:14:44.520 --> 00:14:47.280
I'm a human-yokai kind of yokai!

00:14:47.830 --> 00:14:49.100
<i>What a terrible liar.</i>

00:14:49.100 --> 00:14:50.790
Right, Abeno-san?

00:14:52.130 --> 00:14:55.040
Yeah, that's right. He's human.

00:14:58.630 --> 00:15:03.360
Y-You're the one who told me not 
to let anyone know I'm human!

00:15:03.360 --> 00:15:05.870
Hey, wait! Abeno-san, you're human, too!

00:15:05.870 --> 00:15:07.050
Not so loud!

00:15:07.050 --> 00:15:10.010
Are you abandoning me so you 
can save yourself? That's low!

00:15:10.010 --> 00:15:10.800
Just listen!

00:15:10.800 --> 00:15:12.520
I won't hear your excuses!

00:15:12.520 --> 00:15:14.040
You arrogant! Hot-headed!

00:15:14.040 --> 00:15:15.560
Tyrannical! Scowling!

00:15:15.560 --> 00:15:17.500
Inhuman! Traitor!

00:15:17.500 --> 00:15:20.430
What?! Just try and say that again, Ashiya!

00:15:21.540 --> 00:15:22.760
You're such good friends.

00:15:22.760 --> 00:15:23.960
How do you figure?!

00:15:30.690 --> 00:15:33.600
Is your name Ashiya?

00:15:33.600 --> 00:15:35.700
Huh? Uh, yes...

00:15:38.120 --> 00:15:40.500
<i>Huh? This feels familiar...</i>

00:15:41.010 --> 00:15:44.520
I didn't hire him without reason.

00:15:45.060 --> 00:15:48.510
Besides, if I thought he couldn't do the job,

00:15:49.270 --> 00:15:51.760
I wouldn't have hired him in the first place.

00:15:52.420 --> 00:15:55.370
<i>Abeno-san actually has 
high expectations for me?</i>

00:15:56.140 --> 00:15:59.640
Though, he's a useless failure 
who makes my job harder,

00:15:59.640 --> 00:16:01.500
and he's really irritating.

00:16:01.500 --> 00:16:03.270
<i>Does he expect anything from me?</i>

00:16:03.610 --> 00:16:07.740
If you make a rule that I have to fire him,

00:16:07.740 --> 00:16:09.800
then I can't defy that rule.

00:16:10.390 --> 00:16:11.280
But...

00:16:11.860 --> 00:16:14.000
As long as you don't make it a rule,

00:16:14.000 --> 00:16:15.780
I won't consider firing Ashiya.

00:16:17.750 --> 00:16:19.910
You heard Itsuki.

00:16:20.640 --> 00:16:21.920
What do you think?

00:16:22.730 --> 00:16:28.420
Can a human like you give his body 
and soul in service to yokai?

00:16:29.410 --> 00:16:33.610
<i>Can a human like me work to serve yokai?</i>

00:16:35.490 --> 00:16:36.760
<i>For yokai...</i>

00:16:39.480 --> 00:16:42.710
<i>Am I willing to do all I can for yokai?</i>

00:16:45.040 --> 00:16:46.520
You're right, Legislator.

00:16:46.950 --> 00:16:49.480
I'm not a yokai, but a human.

00:16:50.360 --> 00:16:52.590
But even if I am a human,

00:16:52.590 --> 00:16:55.710
if you asked whether I'd do 
everything I can for humankind,

00:16:55.710 --> 00:16:58.030
I still wouldn't know exactly what you meant.

00:16:58.440 --> 00:16:59.290
Huh?

00:16:59.290 --> 00:17:02.960
I mean, right? Honestly 
speaking, I've never thought

00:17:02.960 --> 00:17:05.100
about doing something for humankind.

00:17:05.100 --> 00:17:09.060
I have no clue what doing something 
for all yokai would mean.

00:17:09.060 --> 00:17:11.600
That's fine, but aren't you 
being a little too honest?

00:17:11.600 --> 00:17:13.030
I suppose you're right.

00:17:14.480 --> 00:17:16.620
There's no way a human like you

00:17:16.620 --> 00:17:19.550
could consider doing anything for yokai.

00:17:21.060 --> 00:17:23.370
It's not that I can't.

00:17:24.440 --> 00:17:29.060
I just can't imagine the scale of something 
as large as "for all yokai."

00:17:30.160 --> 00:17:33.020
I've wanted to help the yokai I've met

00:17:33.020 --> 00:17:35.180
through working at the Mononokean.

00:17:35.600 --> 00:17:36.570
So,

00:17:37.240 --> 00:17:40.010
will you allow me to help with the job

00:17:40.610 --> 00:17:43.080
of exorcising yokai?

00:17:46.200 --> 00:17:49.600
Itsuki, if Ashiya-kun is human, 
that means you're returning

00:17:49.600 --> 00:17:51.230
to the Mundane World, right?

00:17:51.230 --> 00:17:52.410
Huh? Yeah.

00:17:52.410 --> 00:17:54.890
And you're opening a portal to do it.

00:17:54.890 --> 00:17:57.580
"One may only pass between the 
Underworld and Mundane World

00:17:57.580 --> 00:17:59.770
using Underworld portals."

00:18:00.370 --> 00:18:02.500
You made that rule yourself.

00:18:03.360 --> 00:18:06.760
Then I'll make a new rule.

00:18:06.760 --> 00:18:08.680
"Only the master and his employees

00:18:08.680 --> 00:18:12.360
may pass between the Underworld and 
Mundane World using the Mononokean."

00:18:12.750 --> 00:18:15.360
Now you don't have to go to the trouble

00:18:15.360 --> 00:18:18.060
of opening portals for Ashiya-kun.

00:18:18.060 --> 00:18:19.290
Which means...

00:18:19.720 --> 00:18:22.700
I'm relieved you hired such a good employee.

00:18:23.220 --> 00:18:26.880
Oh, good! You discovered I'm human, 
but I don't have to die!

00:18:26.880 --> 00:18:28.220
What? Die?

00:18:28.220 --> 00:18:31.200
It's okay if the Legislator finds out.

00:18:31.200 --> 00:18:34.720
What?! Then you should've said so sooner!

00:18:34.720 --> 00:18:37.340
You wouldn't listen to me, remember?

00:18:37.720 --> 00:18:42.220
The Justice, Executive, 
and I know that Itsuki is human.

00:18:42.220 --> 00:18:44.140
So does Koura.

00:18:44.500 --> 00:18:47.310
Even Koura-san? What about Shizuku-chan?

00:18:47.310 --> 00:18:48.920
She doesn't know.

00:18:48.920 --> 00:18:51.770
Only a handful of yokai know.

00:18:52.400 --> 00:18:54.880
There's no telling what would happen if

00:18:54.880 --> 00:18:56.980
they learned humans were in the Underworld.

00:18:57.360 --> 00:18:59.530
Be careful no one else finds out.

00:18:59.820 --> 00:19:01.030
I will.

00:19:03.440 --> 00:19:04.420
Fuzzy?

00:19:06.210 --> 00:19:07.280
What's wrong, hairball?

00:19:07.280 --> 00:19:08.500
<i>Fuzzy? Hairball?</i>

00:19:11.130 --> 00:19:13.760
You know, I've been wondering...

00:19:13.760 --> 00:19:16.500
Who is this furry yokai?

00:19:17.970 --> 00:19:20.520
Some stuff happened, 
and he got hurt because of us,

00:19:20.520 --> 00:19:22.820
so we'll be nursing him back to health.

00:19:26.000 --> 00:19:27.180
<i>He's full of energy.</i>

00:19:28.120 --> 00:19:28.730
Ow.

00:19:30.260 --> 00:19:32.480
I'm sorry! Are you okay?

00:19:33.120 --> 00:19:35.850
Why did you suddenly freak 
out like that, anyway?

00:19:36.390 --> 00:19:40.420
It seems the hairball had a request for me.

00:19:40.930 --> 00:19:43.110
He wants to work for you, too.

00:19:43.110 --> 00:19:45.620
What? You do?

00:19:46.640 --> 00:19:48.640
Why not? You're hired.

00:19:48.640 --> 00:19:49.530
That was easy!

00:19:49.530 --> 00:19:52.580
You can't just decide that! 
I'm not hiring him!

00:19:53.900 --> 00:19:55.590
Um, Abeno-san...

00:19:56.130 --> 00:20:00.130
You might find it useful 
to have a yokai around.

00:20:01.570 --> 00:20:05.360
Itsuki, "you must hire the 
hairball as an employee."

00:20:05.360 --> 00:20:06.640
"That's a rule."

00:20:06.870 --> 00:20:07.740
Wha—

00:20:10.040 --> 00:20:11.040
Fine.

00:20:11.040 --> 00:20:13.850
Fuzzy, you're hired! Isn't that great?

00:20:20.630 --> 00:20:22.200
You guys go first.

00:20:22.200 --> 00:20:23.200
Okay.

00:20:23.920 --> 00:20:28.110
Come back anytime, Ashiya-kun and hairball.

00:20:28.110 --> 00:20:30.200
We can enjoy some good sake together.

00:20:30.200 --> 00:20:32.860
Oh, I'm underage, actually.

00:20:32.860 --> 00:20:37.420
Oh, you mean the Mundane World's 
"no liquor until you're 20" rule? That's too bad.

00:20:37.420 --> 00:20:38.680
I'll have some juice instead—

00:20:38.680 --> 00:20:41.970
Don't. He'll hold you captive for ten hours.

00:20:42.770 --> 00:20:44.760
Fuzzy, go ahead.

00:20:46.040 --> 00:20:46.950
Itsuki.

00:20:47.640 --> 00:20:48.580
What?

00:20:49.280 --> 00:20:54.260
Sorry for hiring the hairball 
before discussing it with you.

00:20:54.260 --> 00:20:54.940
Right.

00:20:54.940 --> 00:20:56.150
Really, I'm sorry.

00:20:56.460 --> 00:20:58.180
But I understand now.

00:20:58.770 --> 00:21:03.450
You rejected all the yokai
I recommended for employment,

00:21:03.960 --> 00:21:07.660
so I thought you didn't want to hire anyone.

00:21:08.100 --> 00:21:11.660
But you just didn't want to hire a yokai.

00:21:15.680 --> 00:21:19.920
You don't have to worry about a human 
becoming possessed by a parasite shrub.

00:21:20.280 --> 00:21:22.350
Abeno-san, are you coming?

00:21:22.350 --> 00:21:23.420
I'm closing the door.

00:21:23.730 --> 00:21:24.810
Don't close it.

00:21:25.410 --> 00:21:28.930
Don't you think you've become too uptight?

00:21:29.480 --> 00:21:33.000
I don't think what happened was your—

00:21:33.000 --> 00:21:33.900
Legislator.

00:21:36.070 --> 00:21:36.940
Shut up.

00:21:37.410 --> 00:21:38.810
Move! You're in the way!

00:21:38.810 --> 00:21:39.550
Ow!

00:21:39.550 --> 00:21:41.440
Why are you so grumpy all of a sudden?!

00:21:42.230 --> 00:21:43.700
Later, Legislator!

00:21:44.480 --> 00:21:47.450
Even when he's angry, 
he never forgets his goodbyes.

00:21:48.710 --> 00:21:50.450
Honestly...

00:21:51.320 --> 00:21:53.320
What a terrifying master.

00:23:24.960 --> 00:23:39.980
<b>Next Time "The Ring"</b>

00:23:25.930 --> 00:23:29.960
Since Fuzzy joined us, 
now we're the Mononokean Trio!

00:23:29.960 --> 00:23:32.990
Ashiya, the next time you call us 
that, I'm going to knock you out.

00:23:32.990 --> 00:23:35.070
Huh? What's wrong with it?

00:23:35.070 --> 00:23:36.760
The Mononokean Trio!

00:23:36.760 --> 00:23:38.150
I'm knocking you out.
